From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: turboquant <>
Date: Sun, 19 Apr 2026 23:23:36 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] turboquant: add CUDA kernels and GGML ops for TurboQuant KV
 compression
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Adds six new GGML ops and the CUDA kernels that back them. Each op is
CUDA-only; the CPU backend rejects them via
`ggml_backend_cpu_device_supports_op` and the scheduler therefore
never assigns them to a non-GPU split.

New ops (enum `ggml_op`):

  * GGML_OP_TQ_ENCODE       — encodes K to packed N-bit + scale
  * GGML_OP_TQ_DEQUANT      — reconstructs f16 K
  * GGML_OP_TQ_DEQUANT_KV   — back-to-back K and V dequant
  * GGML_OP_TQ_FLASH_ATTN_EXT — fused FA with inline K/V decode (fallback)
  * GGML_OP_TQ_ENCODE_V     — encodes V with optional rotation
  * GGML_OP_TQ_ENCODE_KV    — combined K+V encode in one op

The regular dispatch and op metadata wiring lives in ggml.c /
ggml-backend.cpp / ggml-cpu/ggml-cpu.{c,cpp} / ggml-cuda/ggml-cuda.cu;
the actual CUDA kernels and their launchers live in
src/ggml-cuda/tq-{encode,encode-v,dequant,fattn,fattn-vec}.{cu,cuh}.

The kernels compile under both nvcc and hipcc (ROCm path via the HIP
shim); wave32 gating is enforced on the Go side via scanTQDevices.
